{"adjusted_val_bpb": -2.633875077544463, "attempt": 0, "charged": true, "critic": {"issues": ["No sign of getting around the measurement. There is no file or network access, no pasted coordinates and no use of test labels. All randomness still comes from rng, which is seeded by the seed argument.", "No bug that makes the result meaningless. On a restart, run is set to None and then replaced by the new repaired solution, and stall goes back to 0. Kicks now start from the current run instead of the global best. best is still updated after every repair, so what solve returns is unchanged in kind. The time loop and the repair step are unchanged, so the packing stays valid and the time limit still holds.", "Recomputed z is about -0.355, which matches the reported -0.351; the gap is from the inputs being rounded to 4 decimals. Calculation: (incumbent - candidate) / (0.0023 * sqrt(1/1 + 1/2)) = (-2.6349 + 2.6339) / 0.002817. The candidate's loss is 0.0010 worse, well within noise, so rejecting it is reasonable. The candidate has only one run, so this comparison has little power.", "The diff makes no claims that conflict with the numbers."], "ok": true, "veto": false}, "decision": "reject", "description": "Track a per-run incumbent and a stall counter of non-improving kicks, and after 30 consecutive stalls restart from a fresh random start while keeping the global best; kicks now act on the current run's incumbent.", "edit_class": "structural", "flags": [], "gpu": "willow", "idea_id": "b047", "incumbent_after": {"mean": -2.6348559370198386, "n": 2}, "incumbent_before": {"mean": -2.6348559370198386, "n": 2}, "job_id": "B1_p26_HH_1_s0-candidate-17_1795048619951", "kind": "candidate", "lint": {"hard": [], "ok": true, "warnings": []}, "model_calls": [{"cost_usd_nominal": 0.00263133, "cost_usd_plan": 0.00263133, "latency_s": 10.97395370301092, "requested_model": "haiku", "role": "coder", "served_model": "haiku", "tokens_in": 7331, "tokens_out": 2803}, {"cost_usd_nominal": 0.0258